From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer, shell32: File Explorer follows the app mode, live

In dark mode File Explorer stayed light but for its title bar (QA B19), and
a selected icon's name was white on the light selection tint (B33):
- explorer (fileexplorer.c): the command bar, address bar, navigation pane,
  status bar, This PC page and search results take a light or dark palette
  from HKCU\...\Themes\Personalize AppsUseLightTheme -- when the window is
  made and on WM_SETTINGCHANGE "ImmersiveColorSet" -- and set the title bar
  (DWMWA_USE_IMMERSIVE_DARK_MODE), the tree's and results' colours, and
  repaint. WM_SYSCOLORCHANGE and WM_THEMECHANGED are passed to every child
  control, as Windows programs do (DefWindowProc does not), so the folder
  view's list and header see the dark scheme's colours (0160-0163).
- shell32 (DefView): the selection tint is dark on a dark window
  (COLOR_WINDOW's luminance), so the name, in COLOR_WINDOWTEXT, reads; the
  content view's separator too.

Gate: test/explorer-dark-gate.sh (make test-explorer-dark).
